+# src/features/builtin-skills/ ÔÇö 12 Built-in Skill Files
+
+**Generated:** 2026-05-15
+
+## OVERVIEW
+
+Skills shipped inside the plugin (always available, no install). Registered via `createBuiltinSkills()`. Each skill implements the `BuiltinSkill` interface with name, description, content, and optional MCP config. Loaded by `opencode-skill-loader` with priority: project > opencode > user > **builtin**. User-installed skills with the same name override built-ins.
+
+## STRUCTURE
+
+```
+builtin-skills/
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ index.ts              # Barrel exports
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ skills.ts             # createBuiltinSkills() factory ÔÇö registers all 12 below
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ types.ts              # BuiltinSkill interface
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ skills/
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ git-master.ts                  # 1111 LOC
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ git-master-skill-metadata.ts   # Companion to git-master
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ playwright.ts                  # MCP variant + agent-browser
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ playwright-cli.ts              # CLI variant
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ dev-browser.ts                 # Persistent page state
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ frontend.ts              # Design-first UI guidance
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ review-work.ts                 # 5-agent post-implementation review
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ remove-ai-slops.ts             # Shared skill loader for remove-ai-slops
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ init-deep.ts                   # Shared skill loader for init-deep
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ team-mode.ts                   # 12 team_* tool documentation (gated)
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ security-research.ts           # Team Mode exploitability-driven security research
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ security-review.ts             # Alias for security-research
+Ôöé   Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ git-master-sections/           # Git-master prompt sub-sections
+Ôöé   ÔööÔöÇÔöÇ index.ts                       # skill barrel
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ git-master/                        # Resources for git-master skill
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ frontend/                    # Resources for frontend skill
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ agent-browser/                     # Resources for agent-browser variant
+Ôö£ÔöÇÔöÇ dev-browser/                       # Resources for dev-browser
+ÔööÔöÇÔöÇ security-research/                 # Resources for security-research
+```
+
+## SKILL CATALOG
+
+| Skill | Approx LOC | MCP | Notes |
+|-------|------------|-----|-------|
+| `git-master` | 1111 | ÔÇö | Atomic commits, rebase, history search; included by default for delegate-task `git` category |
+| `playwright` | 312 | `@playwright/mcp` | Browser automation via MCP |
+| `playwright-cli` | 268 | ÔÇö | Browser automation via shell CLI (no MCP) |
+| `agent-browser` | (in playwright.ts) | ÔÇö | Browser via `agent-browser:*` Bash commands |
+| `dev-browser` | 221 | ÔÇö | Persistent page state browser for dev work |
+| `frontend` | 79 | ÔÇö | Design-first UI development guidance |
+| `review-work` | ~500 | ÔÇö | Post-implementation review orchestrator (5 parallel agents) |
+| `$omo:remove-ai-slops` | ÔÇö | ÔÇö | Remove AI-generated code smells |
+| `init-deep` | ÔÇö | ÔÇö | Hierarchical AGENTS.md generation |
+| `security-research` | SKILL.md | ÔÇö | Team Mode exploitability-driven security research |
+| `security-review` | wrapper | ÔÇö | Alias for `security-research` |
+| `team-mode` | ÔÇö | ÔÇö | **Conditional** ÔÇö only loaded when `team_mode.enabled`; documents the 12 `team_*` tools and lifecycle |
+
+## BROWSER VARIANT SELECTION
+
+Config `browser_automation_engine` selects which browser skill loads:
+
+| Value | Skill Loaded |
+|-------|-------------|
+| `"playwright"` (default) | playwright (MCP-backed) |
+| `"playwright-cli"` | playwright-cli (CLI-backed) |
+| `"agent-browser"` | agent-browser (in playwright.ts) |
+
+Only one browser skill is active per session ÔÇö non-selected variants are skipped.
+
+## TEAM-MODE SKILL GATING
+
+The `team-mode` skill is registered unconditionally but only **rendered** when `team_mode.enabled: true`:
+
+```typescript
+// skills/team-mode.ts (paraphrase)
+const teamModeSkill: BuiltinSkill = {
+  name: "team-mode",
+  shouldLoad: (config) => config.team_mode?.enabled === true,
+  // ...
+}
+```
+
+When disabled, the skill is filtered out before agent prompt assembly so agents do not see `team_*` tool docs they cannot use.
+
+## ADDING A NEW BUILT-IN SKILL
+
+1. Create `skills/{name}.ts` exporting a `BuiltinSkill` object
+2. Register in `skills.ts` `createBuiltinSkills()` factory
+3. Add resources (if any) under a sibling directory: `{name}/SKILL.md`, prompt sections, etc.
+4. If the skill is conditional, set `shouldLoad: (config) => ÔÇª`
+5. Optionally declare an MCP server in the skill (loaded by `skill-mcp-manager` per session)
